==Old English==

===Etymology===
{{PIE root|ang|ǵews}}
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*keusaną}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{m|ine-pro|*ǵews-||taste, choose}}.  Cognate with {{etyl|ofs|-}} {{m|ofs|kiāsa}} ({{etyl|fy|-}} {{m|fy|kieze}}), {{etyl|osx|-}} {{m|osx|kiosan}} ({{etyl|nds|-}} {{m|nds|kesen}}), {{etyl|nl|-}} {{m|nl|kiezen}}, {{etyl|goh|-}} {{m|goh|kiosan}}, {{m|goh|chiosan}} ({{etyl|de|-}} {{m|de|kiesen}}), {{etyl|non|-}} {{m|non|kjósa}} ({{etyl|da|-}} {{m|da|kyse}}, {{etyl|is|-}} {{m|is|kjósa}}), {{etyl|got|-}} {{m|got|𐌺𐌹𐌿𐍃𐌰𐌽}}.  The Indo-European root was also the source of {{etyl|la|-}} {{m|la|gustus||taste}}, {{etyl|sq|-}} {{m|sq|desha||chosen}}.

